```js
function makeCounter(start = 0) {
  let count = start;              // private binding.
  return {
    increment: () => ++count,     // closes over count.
    read: () => count,
  };
}

const likes = makeCounter();
const views = makeCounter(100);
likes.increment();                // 1
likes.increment();                // 2
views.increment();                // 101
likes.read();                     // 2: views didn't touch it.
```

| Fact | Consequence |
|---|---|
| inner function keeps outer bindings. | count survives after makeCounter returns. |
| it sees the current value. | read() reports the latest count. |
| each outer call = new bindings. | likes and views are independent. |
| no outside name reaches count. | it is private without a class. |

